
- Clone this repository or add it as a GIT submodule to your own repository as
  a subdirectory named 'tex'.

  Use: 
	$ git submodule init
	$ git submodule update

- Copy the mk directory to the top-level so that BIBINPUTS and TEXTINPUTS point
  to the right directories.

- Put your BibTeX files under the directory 'bib'.


On Windows:

- Use GIT bash to navigate to the top-level then execute:

	source tex/tools/winenv.sh

- Use pdflatex and bibtex as if you were on Unix.

